   "stem": {
      "text": "The function \\( h \\) has derivatives of all orders, and its values at \\( x = 2 \\) are \\( h(2) = -1 \\), \\( h'(2) = 4 \\), \\( h''(2) = 6 \\), \\( h'''(2) = -6 \\), \\( h^{(4)}(2) = 10 \\). Let \\( P \\) be the third-degree Taylor polynomial for \\( h \\) about \\( x = 2 \\). Find the value of \\( P\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\)."
