         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 3 polynomial needs the values through order 3: \\( h(2) = -1 \\), \\( h'(2) = 4 \\), \\( h''(2) = 6 \\), \\( h'''(2) = -6 \\). The value of order 4 is not used.",
         "mathjson": -6
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Divide each by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{-1}{0!} = -1 \\), \\( \\frac{4}{1!} = 4 \\), \\( \\frac{6}{2!} = 3 \\), \\( \\frac{-6}{3!} = -1 \\).",
         "mathjson": -1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Attach \\( (x - 2)^{k} \\) to the coefficient of order \\( k \\): \\( P(x) = -1 + 4(x - 2) + 3(x - 2)^{2} - (x - 2)^{3} \\).",
